Existing test uses `expect(new SettingsBridge().current()).toBe(QUALITY_PRESETS.high)` — identity with the preset table object. If I derive params from `pipelineParamsForProfile`, identity breaks. I could keep the mapping: `profile.id === 'mobile' ? mobileParams : QUALITY_PRESETS[quality]`. That preserves identity for high/medium/low and adds a mobile param object.

Better: add to `QUALITY_PRESETS` a `mobile` entry? No — `QUALITY_PRESETS` is keyed by `QualityPreset` (3 presets). Instead, in perf.ts's `pipelineParamsForProfile`, return `QUALITY_PRESETS[profile.id]` when the profile id is a quality preset, else the derived object. But that requires a runtime import from settings.js in perf.ts → cycle risk: settings.ts doesn't import perf.ts, so no cycle at all! perf.ts imports type from settings.js currently. Making it a value import is fine (one-directional).

So:

```ts
import { QUALITY_PRESETS, type PipelineParams, type QualityPreset } from "./settings.js";

export function pipelineParamsForProfile(profile: PerfProfile): PipelineParams {
  const preset = QUALITY_PRESETS[profile.id as QualityPreset];
  if (preset !== undefined) return preset;
  return { ...mobile-ish derived... };
}
```

That keeps identity semantics for the three presets.

Now update settingsBridge to hold the effective profile:

```ts
export interface SettingsBridgeOptions { signals?: DeviceSignals }
class SettingsBridge {
  private quality: QualityPreset = DEFAULT_SETTINGS.quality;
  private profile: PerfProfile = PERF_PROFILES.high;
  private params: PipelineParams = QUALITY_PRESETS.high;
  private signals: DeviceSignals;
  apply(settings: Settings): void {
    const profile = profileForSettings(settings, this.signals);
    const params = pipelineParamsForProfile(profile);
    if (params === this.params) return;
    ... notify with (next, prev) and store profile/quality
  }
  profile(): PerfProfile
  quality(): QualityPreset
  setSignals(signals)  // used by tests/dev seams
}
```

Careful: `quality()` currently derives from params identity. With profileForSettings, for `deviceProfile: 'desktop'` the profile is `perfProfileFor(quality)`, so `profile.id === quality`. For mobile, quality stays the stored preset. I'll store quality explicitly in `apply`.

Also `settingsBridge.subscribe` listener in fx/registry.ts does `fxRegistry.setProfile(perfProfileFor(settingsBridge.quality()))` — should become `fxRegistry.setProfile(settingsBridge.profile())` to honor mobile caps. Update that.

Let me write it.

